783381357b900d75df425" :answer-field/choices ["q-320450/field-7/2f4a8327029b03da8f8afc132759dda7a70ededaadd9c5c454614983e04742c5" "q-320450/field-7/eeb25e6ee46efe76df6612068ad424d7f545dd3797a783381357b900d75df425"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320450" :question/id #uuid "846b7b32-8c59-58bd-a480-321017b6d1b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-320450" :question/problem "Determine whether the following differential equation is exact:\n\n$$\n(4+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x+(x{e}^{xy}+3y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nA differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it satisfies the condition\n\n$$\n\\,{{field-1}},\n$$\n\nFor the equation $(4+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x+(x{e}^{xy}+3y)\\,\\text{d}y=0$, we have  \n\n$$\nP=\\,{{field-2}},\n$$\n\n$$\nQ=\\,{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}},\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\,{{field-6}},\n$$\n\n the equation {{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor the equation $(4+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x+(x{e}^{xy}+3y)\\,\\text{d}y=0$, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=4+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy},\\,Q(x,y)=x{e}^{xy}+3y.\n$$\n\nNow, compute the partial derivatives carefully:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,(4+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =2y{e}^{xy}+x{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,(x{e}^{xy}+3y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x},\n$$\n\nso the exactness condition fails. Therefore, the given differential equation $\\text{is not exact}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320450/field-1" "q-320450/field-2" "q-320450/field-3" "q-320450/field-4" "q-320450/field-5" "q-320450/field-6" "q-320450/field-7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df3a798c-f226-5b4f-8d65-4a305de2b087"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "69da71c6-0818-56c1-be1b-d88e3521bc19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b6aa73c0-6eb9-5adb-89f6-5b0d4cbbc7a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "afc1c2f7-83af-587a-acf0-7e2f5c77ab81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175/selection/ff8b9a597ddd381e464bcd0770da0fa8c36469448f44d35bc5b3a4fbbde75076" :answer/id #uuid "73d38f31-1e4d-5a7b-85ee-854c352ef12c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f68954f9-c3be-586c-9ea2-344b3c3e73d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d81e09e-2d7a-590b-af64-82f21f2a36ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103175/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-103175/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-103175/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103175/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103175/selection/ff8b9a597ddd381e464bcd0770da0fa8c36469448f44d35bc5b3a4fbbde75076" "q-103175/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103175" :question/id #uuid "368064cc-9b0a-544e-bc34-335b8aa95f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-103175" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\n- ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$\n- $-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\n- ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2})=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2})=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-2y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''I only''." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103175/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64207"] :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+8$\n- $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-2$\n- $2x+7$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=4{y}^{3}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{y}^{3})=0\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+8.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+8)=0=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+8$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-3)=0=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-3$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=2x+7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+7)=0=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2x+7$ gives an exact equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bf5fcd89-355f-5aea-8bf6-bead093bda0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "47ea3880-97d6-5695-959f-c6691bd2a8be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8670f68b-2cbd-50cb-a4c3-411f8bf23928" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "8418349a-7031-59ca-9349-9aa519acc2be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9de6bd51-13cf-58cd-806d-a3d3e528aa7b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f23bfff-97f3-5e5d-beb8-38983083c3ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103172/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-103172/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103172/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-103172/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103172/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-103172/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103172" :question/id #uuid "d0e84f03-1d6a-5d04-a139-0cf3f851d753" :question/math-academy-id "q-103172" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n\n- $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$\n- $3{y}^{2}$\n- $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂x}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $Q(x,y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y).$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $Q(x,y)=3{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2})=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3{y}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1))=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$ gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103172/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103172"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8ff21e5d-19ce-5a3e-afec-3832a5acf685" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e6788963-2536-54dd-a248-42342d8e26d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c6a231f1-fa72-5f22-8309-d138e41d4c0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "05f7d98a-ecdf-5517-a50c-7d92e8c3f799" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "01c7cef0-dd72-5f38-a26d-3d93a2e2af71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d64997-7ece-5ca0-b47d-4e64db5be222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90493/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-90493/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-90493/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-90493/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-90493/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-90493/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90493" :question/id #uuid "8fa44e0d-f47d-55dc-9787-703e1dcaa8bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-90493" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+5{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\n- $10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4$\n- $2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y$\n- $2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=5{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{y}^{4}{e}^{2x})=10{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4)=50{y}^{4}{e}^{x}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y)=10{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}-1\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x})=10{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x}$ gives an exact equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90493/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90493"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "3454ba12-5cb8-5dc0-88cf-7685227e3a61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "52cedde0-0bbf-5e75-9b9e-1a91c171b12b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "980a631b-e920-5150-bd25-a05d11769f53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "37d56f4f-789e-5f7d-91ce-c6c312c7c28b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c97a74aa-f9ed-59b5-bc0d-a025f921e91b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b757bc7-03fd-5243-90e7-459c930e796f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103174/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-103174/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-103174/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103174/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-103174/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103174/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103174" :question/id #uuid "a5f4a045-5343-5261-852f-034babd8107f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103174" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n\n- $6x{y}^{2}$\n- $3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$\n- $2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y)=2x{y}^{3}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{3})=6x{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂x}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $Q(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6x{y}^{2})=6{y}^{2}\\ne \\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6x{y}^{2}=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{3}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\ne \\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''II only''." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103174/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103174"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219/selection/b1733b4f99b88a56b609fbc6355a99c58e987056938145817b066408a9374954" :answer/id #uuid "c0828ce7-df15-517a-b61e-125f134075d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+y}{2}+xy=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219/selection/e0f8c321c849d271dd49deac35e1c46235c6953a51f99d98ef3aeb3e6bc5890a" :answer/id #uuid "ad7375cd-4277-5ccf-8ed0-75ceb660e33c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}-{x}^{3}y=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219/selection/ca49f640edef1a1924bcb6173ee604d990cd5a47fbd2b6167a289501a020df20" :answer/id #uuid "242114e4-4c79-5d2c-9526-c2eb4c3c39db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}y+xy=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219/selection/d343bf52b566587844d2d6acc92ced8979240d5c52f1f6c5df2300f2f3aea02a" :answer/id #uuid "cfc4bf10-6ef9-58a4-8f6d-b4ed6346599a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{y}{x}=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219/selection/d4f7410ae25ed42ff45473a8872beac45753b863927ea5b4d03cb2bdc44ef182" :answer/id #uuid "63ab6ad1-6d6f-5d59-8eb6-f3fe657f6ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-4xy+{y}^{3}=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "607ee7d2-e666-5db6-a456-72bc2f3083f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64219/selection/e0f8c321c849d271dd49deac35e1c46235c6953a51f99d98ef3aeb3e6bc5890a" :answer-field/choices ["q-64219/selection/b1733b4f99b88a56b609fbc6355a99c58e987056938145817b066408a9374954" "q-64219/selection/e0f8c321c849d271dd49deac35e1c46235c6953a51f99d98ef3aeb3e6bc5890a" "q-64219/selection/ca49f640edef1a1924bcb6173ee604d990cd5a47fbd2b6167a289501a020df20" "q-64219/selection/d343bf52b566587844d2d6acc92ced8979240d5c52f1f6c5df2300f2f3aea02a" "q-64219/selection/d4f7410ae25ed42ff45473a8872beac45753b863927ea5b4d03cb2bdc44ef182"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64219" :question/id #uuid "5a52d91e-ac3b-5e2e-8961-60194ab9ab09" :question/math-academy-id "q-64219" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n(4x+3{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+(6xy-{x}^{3})\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=4x+3{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)=6xy-{x}^{3}.$\n\nLet's check if the equation is exact. To do this, we check to see if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x+3{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}y)=6y-3{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy-{x}^{3})=6y-3{x}^{2}=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the given equation is exact and its solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (4x+3{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}-{x}^{3}y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (6xy-{x}^{3})\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =3x{y}^{2}-{x}^{3}y+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=2{x}^{2},\\,f(y)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}-{x}^{3}y=c.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64219/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cbd51b4-cbd1-5e18-8c49-44be7967cd38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64215"] :question/problem "Find the solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(4+y)\\text{d}x+(x+{e}^{y})\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the initial condition $y(0)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=4+y$ and $Q(x,y)=x+{e}^{y}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (4+y)\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =4x+xy+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x+{e}^{y})\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =xy+{e}^{y}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=4x,\\,f(y)={e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n4x+xy+{e}^{y}=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=1$ when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+xy+{e}^{y} & =c \\\\ 4(0)+(0)(1)+{e}^{1} & =c \\\\ c & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n4x+xy+{e}^{y}=e.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339/selection/d4308948c1e80cda9012b3bfac58412b81d9a4e7f286ce809f14dfc9821698b4" :answer/id #uuid "c6945420-0d23-5961-903f-42baee96a523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339/selection/df8a46148408e9014c7b787d3a68dcc9765db1c5dee92395fda54b575224a7fe" :answer/id #uuid "10339ce0-c7f3-5f0c-9725-0455f672610c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339/selection/1536ab94354cc981e3b0aef8b6d527a035003d4e060ba0d966282eac26793311" :answer/id #uuid "14466c2d-4181-5d2a-baeb-43f48fc28e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339/selection/a85b8765edf7d68dea1b3abd60a7846444954b8d78c95e94bd7dca8ffb2f464a" :answer/id #uuid "ce27ece8-be33-5639-a6af-9cba4f8c3599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339/selection/a3242f24d669aae0f957e357fc3de5846925e77cc6d3cfcba6855cd8d9f36e03" :answer/id #uuid "8d14d9d4-ed81-53f0-9bf7-297b72faf2ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d837d48f-c18e-5cbf-8d52-241827191488" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103339/selection/a3242f24d669aae0f957e357fc3de5846925e77cc6d3cfcba6855cd8d9f36e03" :answer-field/choices ["q-103339/selection/d4308948c1e80cda9012b3bfac58412b81d9a4e7f286ce809f14dfc9821698b4" "q-103339/selection/df8a46148408e9014c7b787d3a68dcc9765db1c5dee92395fda54b575224a7fe" "q-103339/selection/1536ab94354cc981e3b0aef8b6d527a035003d4e060ba0d966282eac26793311" "q-103339/selection/a85b8765edf7d68dea1b3abd60a7846444954b8d78c95e94bd7dca8ffb2f464a" "q-103339/selection/a3242f24d669aae0f957e357fc3de5846925e77cc6d3cfcba6855cd8d9f36e03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103339" :question/id #uuid "f7949606-3a7a-5b98-8e86-415afaf09dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103339" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(3{y}^{2}-6{x}^{2}y)\\,\\text{d}x+(6xy-2{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(1)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=3{y}^{2}-6{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)=6xy-2{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (3{y}^{2}-6{x}^{2}y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (6xy-2{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=0,\\,f(y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=0$ when $x=1.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=c \\\\ 3\\cdot (1)\\cdot (0)^{2}-2\\cdot (1)^{3}\\cdot (0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=c \\\\ 0+0+1=c \\\\ c=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n3x{y}^{2}-2{x}^{3}y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103339/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cbd51b4-cbd1-5e18-8c49-44be7967cd38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211/selection/26155e613938bb92c80c307f741ad580236acf24873be5e14d1829bd40e42583" :answer/id #uuid "7e0369cd-3132-58eb-afc0-2f91772d385c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}y+1)}{4}+xy=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211/selection/f639b06d5f5bdf15b0011de3a97148d0d37d0cdce8495ccfd672fa8ada2af011" :answer/id #uuid "70654121-6936-5fa5-9c45-aed55859b838" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211/selection/256ecc0b0200ae2f5f04f2ef9ee17f4332126fb923697f4f6490a2271bb7a788" :answer/id #uuid "31ce7042-533e-5557-b52c-ecc0575d8cfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}y-6xy+x{y}^{3}=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211/selection/246078d4c99cf58ea39d2bf190fa0feaf75a1d54b454b919ead4292b36032d77" :answer/id #uuid "43b63bc5-7955-57e0-88b2-75609347df18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+xy+{y}^{2}=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211/selection/0e1fad6f49ff8904ed0b77eaff1a4b898dac1b3c16f9d58004f0dde0594e6390" :answer/id #uuid "b6fdcdf7-c9c8-5ed5-bc50-1fa6445d36b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}+2)+{y}^{3}=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad2b93b4-a690-57da-93b4-e32a0707e738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64211/selection/f639b06d5f5bdf15b0011de3a97148d0d37d0cdce8495ccfd672fa8ada2af011" :answer-field/choices ["q-64211/selection/26155e613938bb92c80c307f741ad580236acf24873be5e14d1829bd40e42583" "q-64211/selection/f639b06d5f5bdf15b0011de3a97148d0d37d0cdce8495ccfd672fa8ada2af011" "q-64211/selection/256ecc0b0200ae2f5f04f2ef9ee17f4332126fb923697f4f6490a2271bb7a788" "q-64211/selection/246078d4c99cf58ea39d2bf190fa0feaf75a1d54b454b919ead4292b36032d77" "q-64211/selection/0e1fad6f49ff8904ed0b77eaff1a4b898dac1b3c16f9d58004f0dde0594e6390"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64211" :question/id #uuid "da33770a-9c81-5d44-ae0b-5a300064b2f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-64211" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}+2{y}^{3})\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{3}+2{y}^{3}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 3{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{3}+2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=0,\\,f(y)=\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}=c.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64211/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cbd51b4-cbd1-5e18-8c49-44be7967cd38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341/selection/98a93e273d9d6eb63b232b54a942238f03b64d45cf2bbe06911788a23967249e" :answer/id #uuid "e67894ba-728a-5bea-8e2a-5af1a80247a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341/selection/7053570f5023e193f83af680abec3a0ac1d929359c0ea1bd7334ac527b5f680d" :answer/id #uuid "090c95eb-400e-5640-8e37-35a80ef250e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341/selection/537e4e78b3366dff18ccc13eed501057d0824062b24dc23f86a03537372a90ad" :answer/id #uuid "da460d15-c407-50eb-85bf-be68a009abc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341/selection/ce7861b0c3e5d20eeb0e53b242d7620bb54ba97609819cbabc38c63de2e2e4bd" :answer/id #uuid "a6d7d1a2-a14f-540e-884c-681bf42c5096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341/selection/cefd40d6b5964e11765ee34eb3f14d50e9e5240c12228e208715f51b8653c133" :answer/id #uuid "26d8eda3-5972-54b2-b2e4-42cd31190752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ca6fb9-3fc5-51de-8620-5dbf05bb13ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103341/selection/98a93e273d9d6eb63b232b54a942238f03b64d45cf2bbe06911788a23967249e" :answer-field/choices ["q-103341/selection/98a93e273d9d6eb63b232b54a942238f03b64d45cf2bbe06911788a23967249e" "q-103341/selection/7053570f5023e193f83af680abec3a0ac1d929359c0ea1bd7334ac527b5f680d" "q-103341/selection/537e4e78b3366dff18ccc13eed501057d0824062b24dc23f86a03537372a90ad" "q-103341/selection/ce7861b0c3e5d20eeb0e53b242d7620bb54ba97609819cbabc38c63de2e2e4bd" "q-103341/selection/cefd40d6b5964e11765ee34eb3f14d50e9e5240c12228e208715f51b8653c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103341" :question/id #uuid "e2d85391-9596-5c36-a133-a6a5b4d8cd71" :question/math-academy-id "q-103341" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x+(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\frac{1}{y})\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\frac{1}{y}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\frac{1}{y})\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\,f(y)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy) & =c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103341/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cbd51b4-cbd1-5e18-8c49-44be7967cd38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103341"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203/selection/dd1843d0da889ca9466b6ca922344cd6d59479ae7f19990f2ecc1b5226c36f56" :answer/id #uuid "d3d2cfc6-d096-5cdd-825d-4ada79a91e21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-2x+2y=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203/selection/cd88ec1e29de6476744b8971aa9937ada4ed4e96300e93e04c6d491701d6b8ce" :answer/id #uuid "304ea185-b4be-5d00-a2df-75147084b4dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-{x}^{2}+2x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203/selection/0bb8228bbfde99f3b23d55d92509096c020006e4dddf18ade8eb3977d5159945" :answer/id #uuid "b4de7c67-e8fa-5a25-9166-7d12b340ee48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{2}+2x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203/selection/77c12835a9aedfed4dc17518110d3e9f693bfcdfa0c1b29938b4a34cbfc63066" :answer/id #uuid "190998d1-3d98-5c20-a456-40ddfec83ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-{x}^{2}+2y=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203/selection/5e65d6ed1627b617de40c4c7afabf25c257e0a5fe5088b1242d51ed703f2162f" :answer/id #uuid "bef42a54-156f-5a7e-8d09-0a38ab07daff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-x+2y=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e761f5a2-3489-576e-9320-c6d1c49120de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-321203/selection/0bb8228bbfde99f3b23d55d92509096c020006e4dddf18ade8eb3977d5159945" :answer-field/choices ["q-321203/selection/dd1843d0da889ca9466b6ca922344cd6d59479ae7f19990f2ecc1b5226c36f56" "q-321203/selection/cd88ec1e29de6476744b8971aa9937ada4ed4e96300e93e04c6d491701d6b8ce" "q-321203/selection/0bb8228bbfde99f3b23d55d92509096c020006e4dddf18ade8eb3977d5159945" "q-321203/selection/77c12835a9aedfed4dc17518110d3e9f693bfcdfa0c1b29938b4a34cbfc63066" "q-321203/selection/5e65d6ed1627b617de40c4c7afabf25c257e0a5fe5088b1242d51ed703f2162f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321203" :question/id #uuid "fbbaa42a-3568-545a-bdcc-23f3e75863ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-321203" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5}}{2y-{x}^{5}{y}^{4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5}}{2y-{x}^{5}{y}^{4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(2y-{x}^{5}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(2y-{x}^{5}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y=(2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we  rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{5}{y}^{4}-2y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5},\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{5}{y}^{4}-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5}) \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}{y}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{5}{y}^{4}-2y) \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}{y}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (2+{x}^{4}{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{5}{y}^{4}-2y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=2x,\\,f(y)=-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{5}{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{2}+2x=c.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321203/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb08d6e-ae86-50f5-8cb4-d7fe50595849"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321203"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147/selection/237ccdbaa41b819903ead09a27cdaea6c4bae726b8b1be2ae832e10262274eaf" :answer/id #uuid "61a072ef-0085-5927-aee8-4471ee4d89d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({y}^{2}+3x){e}^{xy}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147/selection/9f4d26233b6e71492dbec73b97e553d9a939b263345a73aaa384094f9c95e68e" :answer/id #uuid "d7e295a6-c219-5315-8799-df81d3e3d181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{xy}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+3x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147/selection/a47117920484b64cd8ff016e11fabd27c2bd55f48e697dbdf8b650c05e74a309" :answer/id #uuid "48a270fb-0aa0-51af-a02d-c388ceda65c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{xy}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+3x=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147/selection/d0c8380eb5d88e28fc2cf65b368a776204cdb27a0ee65675318291e5f1704e22" :answer/id #uuid "8315fe9a-0653-5303-ba33-a2a9362383ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{xy}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+3x=\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147/selection/70bf994284e2fb55be1fdd103e5c282c49ad4c4b8b718696470bc94a1848e84c" :answer/id #uuid "c4b2f705-448f-5d3c-98bb-64132e7e4487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}+{e}^{xy}+3x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c38c8f6-ed44-5451-a1f4-d420d3162da7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-321147/selection/d0c8380eb5d88e28fc2cf65b368a776204cdb27a0ee65675318291e5f1704e22" :answer-field/choices ["q-321147/selection/237ccdbaa41b819903ead09a27cdaea6c4bae726b8b1be2ae832e10262274eaf" "q-321147/selection/9f4d26233b6e71492dbec73b97e553d9a939b263345a73aaa384094f9c95e68e" "q-321147/selection/a47117920484b64cd8ff016e11fabd27c2bd55f48e697dbdf8b650c05e74a309" "q-321147/selection/d0c8380eb5d88e28fc2cf65b368a776204cdb27a0ee65675318291e5f1704e22" "q-321147/selection/70bf994284e2fb55be1fdd103e5c282c49ad4c4b8b718696470bc94a1848e84c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321147" :question/id #uuid "fb0676b3-5de0-51bf-9a0b-81cfc80be52a" :question/math-academy-id "q-321147" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{3+4y\\,{e}^{xy}}{3y-4x\\,{e}^{xy}},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(0)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3+4y\\,{e}^{xy}}{3y-4x\\,{e}^{xy}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(3y-4x\\,{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(3y-4x\\,{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}y=(3+4y\\,{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(3+4y\\,{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x+(4x\\,{e}^{xy}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3+4y\\,{e}^{xy},\\,Q(x,y)=4x\\,{e}^{xy}-3y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3+4y\\,{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{xy}+4xy\\,{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\,{e}^{xy}-3y) \\\\  & =4{e}^{xy}+4xy\\,{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (3+4y\\,{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =3x+4{e}^{xy}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (4x\\,{e}^{xy}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =4{e}^{xy}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=3x,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n4{e}^{xy}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+3x=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=1$ when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{xy}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+3x & =c \\\\ 4{e}^{0\\cdot 1}-\\frac{3}{2}(1)^{2}+3\\cdot 0 & =c \\\\ c & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n4{e}^{xy}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+3x=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321147/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb08d6e-ae86-50f5-8cb4-d7fe50595849"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321147"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586/selection/9d4a3cb9ee25ec6ac7c249ae7608387afdb58e9db9f2f16d044e5ac71bee4950" :answer/id #uuid "4e4036dd-e83a-5933-9347-609b6797dfd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-5x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586/selection/f1aadae69806c0fd20997226403299211b91139eafaabde2fc9b002e952224d1" :answer/id #uuid "59c486a6-fba5-5c52-bec5-7c31927e2617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-5x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586/selection/e38f2d83ba731a1315d7d275b26681284688916284643de2c88b7a5032fb70eb" :answer/id #uuid "56bd45c9-197a-5393-b0f1-568ee4ba8e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({y}^{2}-5x)\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586/selection/48bec48161fa65eab7b9fa91f1c222b4ff286f7e4331bfb3c716d3182f17f9f0" :answer/id #uuid "018801e3-a35a-5324-a90b-6a16702969ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+2{y}^{2}+5x=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586/selection/206e116346b6dff0ccfe9c217c935a108144ebe018eefb0fdb8ce464abcd8dbb" :answer/id #uuid "c058c67f-ecc8-5cec-94de-69359cf44a72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x=-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf00bbf6-0040-55ba-ad7c-dcdb06503f06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-320586/selection/206e116346b6dff0ccfe9c217c935a108144ebe018eefb0fdb8ce464abcd8dbb" :answer-field/choices ["q-320586/selection/9d4a3cb9ee25ec6ac7c249ae7608387afdb58e9db9f2f16d044e5ac71bee4950" "q-320586/selection/f1aadae69806c0fd20997226403299211b91139eafaabde2fc9b002e952224d1" "q-320586/selection/e38f2d83ba731a1315d7d275b26681284688916284643de2c88b7a5032fb70eb" "q-320586/selection/48bec48161fa65eab7b9fa91f1c222b4ff286f7e4331bfb3c716d3182f17f9f0" "q-320586/selection/206e116346b6dff0ccfe9c217c935a108144ebe018eefb0fdb8ce464abcd8dbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320586" :question/id #uuid "c1a886d5-cc15-576c-812c-a1301ce1d5ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-320586" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5}{\\,4y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(0)=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5}{4y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(4y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(4y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\,\\text{d}y=(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5)\\,\\text{d}x+(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5,\\,Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+5x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=5x,\\,f(y)=-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=-2$ when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0\\cdot (-2))-2(-2)^{2}+5\\cdot 0 & =c \\\\ c & =0-8 \\\\ c & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x=-8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320586/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb08d6e-ae86-50f5-8cb4-d7fe50595849"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589/selection/3cf797a4ef8eb47317c5d8ed004037b134f04cbcda46006794ebdc00f737e7ba" :answer/id #uuid "7aa2716d-21e4-56db-957c-b4811bb40a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}+{e}^{xy}-5x=17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589/selection/aa009d268cd23b86d4d36553069b182cc208eb9c7e9f3198afb6467b763a51ae" :answer/id #uuid "3d437b16-2617-5496-bb06-a5e9ad53a03e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{xy}-2{y}^{2}-5x=-31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589/selection/957abf0fa148b39c093ab006d38ba0bdd640c4b302f64ceb33b52b1a126c7fc9" :answer/id #uuid "b5273aa0-9393-5e2c-acc3-19782d9d7065" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({y}^{2}+5x)\\,{e}^{xy}=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589/selection/e6a0851008892151fa9e0e60aa277ec365745a881ecfcddb719cfeec11c3a031" :answer/id #uuid "a1ed2965-aa2e-59d6-90f2-9b2866e7fb94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}-{e}^{xy}+5x=15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589/selection/081c89ca705435cfdd76d134c69c0889a85af7918ec346b990582e44fd453eb9" :answer/id #uuid "c8b169e8-13f3-5741-9755-7c322bbf6dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{xy}+2{y}^{2}+5x=33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb5605f-0df2-5ffd-b486-47d82ddb61d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-320589/selection/aa009d268cd23b86d4d36553069b182cc208eb9c7e9f3198afb6467b763a51ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-320589/selection/3cf797a4ef8eb47317c5d8ed004037b134f04cbcda46006794ebdc00f737e7ba" "q-320589/selection/aa009d268cd23b86d4d36553069b182cc208eb9c7e9f3198afb6467b763a51ae" "q-320589/selection/957abf0fa148b39c093ab006d38ba0bdd640c4b302f64ceb33b52b1a126c7fc9" "q-320589/selection/e6a0851008892151fa9e0e60aa277ec365745a881ecfcddb719cfeec11c3a031" "q-320589/selection/081c89ca705435cfdd76d134c69c0889a85af7918ec346b990582e44fd453eb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320589" :question/id #uuid "817973e7-579b-5512-9e78-4ff1bd0baf95" :question/math-academy-id "q-320589" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{y{e}^{xy}-5}{\\,4y-x{e}^{xy}\\,},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(0)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y{e}^{xy}-5}{4y-x{e}^{xy}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(4y-x{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(4y-x{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}y=(y{e}^{xy}-5)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(y{e}^{xy}-5)\\,\\text{d}x+(x{e}^{xy}-4y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}-5,\\,Q(x,y)=x{e}^{xy}-4y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy}-5) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{xy}-4y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (y{e}^{xy}-5)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}-5x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x{e}^{xy}-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}-2{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=-5x,\\,f(y)=-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{e}^{xy}-2{y}^{2}-5x=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=4$ when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy}-2{y}^{2}-5x & =c \\\\ {e}^{0\\cdot 4}-2(4)^{2}-5\\cdot 0 & =c \\\\ c & =1-32 \\\\ c & =-31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n{e}^{xy}-2{y}^{2}-5x=-31.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb08d6e-ae86-50f5-8cb4-d7fe50595849"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585/selection/edd187d6b978bd7558d91c29b2249faedfea5924cfd3d250528f1ad74d82167e" :answer/id #uuid "df38a237-9f28-5661-b80e-89ca574e2115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+{y}^{2}-3x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585/selection/e7435013671527943398bbfe71a63908f28b1241bf82c0772588f68718ab413e" :answer/id #uuid "ee45b6a8-a835-5881-961e-c9080ac2450c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({y}^{2}-3x)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585/selection/68e546affa12e01f5a1b8ac17a2a8c85ea07d2bd5ba34b3d48fbcbe9916d4cef" :answer/id #uuid "e07b09e6-b87d-59e2-8453-ca81ba6f50ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)-1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585/selection/9d8b873540753ea9690ba270ca43de438365212fca8797e3c50c15fe6b0655ee" :answer/id #uuid "fa9b6e15-8e9f-5d90-aeef-26c7440e3b03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{y}^{2}+3x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585/selection/53fd02b13c961ee4777b45b4c25d9c82c7ae919f987ea621b416724d13c3bc96" :answer/id #uuid "6560f956-6faf-516d-b75d-a14cdbe43d27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-3x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "871a2ced-dbfb-578c-849e-d5a1208fba1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-320585/selection/9d8b873540753ea9690ba270ca43de438365212fca8797e3c50c15fe6b0655ee" :answer-field/choices ["q-320585/selection/edd187d6b978bd7558d91c29b2249faedfea5924cfd3d250528f1ad74d82167e" "q-320585/selection/e7435013671527943398bbfe71a63908f28b1241bf82c0772588f68718ab413e" "q-320585/selection/68e546affa12e01f5a1b8ac17a2a8c85ea07d2bd5ba34b3d48fbcbe9916d4cef" "q-320585/selection/9d8b873540753ea9690ba270ca43de438365212fca8797e3c50c15fe6b0655ee" "q-320585/selection/53fd02b13c961ee4777b45b4c25d9c82c7ae919f987ea621b416724d13c3bc96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320585" :question/id #uuid "806a537b-2d39-5ccf-b479-d935eaaf7929" :question/math-academy-id "q-320585" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3}{\\,2y-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(0)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3}{\\,2y-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by$(2y-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(2y-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))\\,\\text{d}y=(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3)\\,\\text{d}x+(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3,\\,Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+3)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+3x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=3x,\\,f(y)=-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{y}^{2}+3x=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=1$  when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{y}^{2}+3x & =c \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0\\cdot 1)-(1)^{2}+3\\cdot 0 & =c \\\\ c & =-1-1 \\\\ c & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{y}^{2}+3x=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb08d6e-ae86-50f5-8cb4-d7fe50595849"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-20933"] :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is exact?  \n\n- $(2xy)\\,\\textrm{d}x + (x^{2}+4)\\,\\textrm{d}y = 0$\n\n- $(y^{2}+2x)\\,\\textrm{d}x + (xy+1)\\,\\textrm{d}y = 0$\n\n- $(7y - x)\\,\\textrm{d}y - (y - 3x)\\,\\textrm{d}x = 0$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\textrm{d}x +Q(x,y)\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation:\n\n- The first equation is\n\n$$\n(2xy)\\;\\textrm{d}x + (x^{2}+4)\\;\\textrm{d}y = 0.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y) = 2xy, \\qquad Q(x,y) = x^{2}+4.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} {=} \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}. \\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\n \nThus, equation I is exact.\n\n- The second equation is\n\n$$\n(y^{2}+2x)\\;\\textrm{d}x + (xy+1)\\;\\textrm{d}y = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y) = y^{2}+2x, \\qquad Q(x,y) = xy+1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+1) \\\\  & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} {\\neq} \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}. \\quad{\\color{red}{\\times}}\n$$\n\nThus, equation II is not exact.\n\n- The third equation is\n\n$$\n(7y - x)\\;\\textrm{d}y - (y - 3x)\\;\\textrm{d}x = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y) = -(y - 3x) = 3x - y, \\qquad Q(x,y) = 7y - x.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x-y) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(7y-x) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} {=} \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}. \\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\nThus, equation III is exact.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-20894"] :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{y}{ x^2 } \\textrm{d}x + Q(x,y)\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n\n- $\\dfrac{1}{x}$\n\n- $\\dfrac{y}{x}$\n\n- $e^{yx}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\textrm{d}x +Q(x,y)\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y) = -\\dfrac{y}{x^2}.$\n\n First, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} =\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(-\\dfrac{y}{x^2}\\right)=-\\dfrac{1}{x^2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}$ to each of the given options and determine whether the results match up with $\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}$ above:\n\n- If $Q(x,y) = \\dfrac{1}{x},$ then we get an exact equation:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\dfrac 1 x\\right) = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2} = \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} \\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\n- If $Q(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x},$ then we do *not* get an exact equation:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\dfrac y x\\right) = -\\dfrac{y}{x^2} \\neq \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} \\quad{\\color{red}{\\times}}\n$$\n\n- If $Q(x,y) = e^{xy},$ then we do *not* get an exact equation:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(e^{xy}\\right) = ye^{xy} \\neq \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} \\quad{\\color{red}{\\times}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-20895"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(y^2-2x)\\,\\textrm{d}x + (2xy +1)\\textrm{d}y = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\textrm{d}x +Q(x,y)\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y) = y^2-2x$ and $Q(x,y) = 2xy+1.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = P(x,y),\\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} = Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int {y}^{2}-2x\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y$.  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int 2xy+1\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}+y+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x) = -x^2, \\qquad f(y) = y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y) = c$ is\n\n$$\nxy^2-x^2 + y = c.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-20934"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\ny' = \\frac{11+ye^{xy}}{13y - xe^{xy}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\textrm{d}x +Q(x,y)\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{11+y{e}^{xy}}{13y-x{e}^{xy}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(13y-xe^{xy})\\;\\textrm{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(13y-xe^{xy})\\;\\textrm{d}y = (11+ye^{xy})\\;\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we then rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(11+ye^{xy})\\;\\textrm{d}x + (xe^{xy}-13y)\\;\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\textrm{d}x +Q(x,y)\\textrm{d}y = 0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y) =11+ye^{xy}, \\qquad Q(x,y) = xe^{xy}-13y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(11+y{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{xy}-13y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} {=} \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}. \\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = P(x,y),\\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} = Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (11+y{e}^{xy})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =11x+{e}^{xy}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x{e}^{xy}-13y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x) = 11x, \\quad  f(y) = - \\dfrac{13}{2}y^2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y) = c$ is\n\n$$\ne^{xy} - \\dfrac{13}{2}y^2 + 11x = c.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
